<title>USA: Washington Mutual offering begins trading.</title>
<headline>Washington Mutual offering begins trading.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>A secondary common stock offering by Washington Mutual Savings Bank began trading on Thursday, according to lead underwriter Merrill Lynch.</p>
<p>The stock was the second most actively traded on Nasdaq at midmorning, with 4.4 million shares trading up one to 49-1/2.</p>
<p>The offering of 14,589,649 shares was priced at $47.50 and declared effective by the Securities and Exchange Commission on Wednesday.</p>
